{#
  The joke desk: one short joke on each of the day's biggest stories, read across BOTH newsrooms
  (regional and world news from Nord-Norge, national politics from the satire desk). The humour is
  built on George Carlin's method -- soft language, the club, the premise taken literally, scale,
  the list -- see templates/vitsedesken.md.

  This filters on reports.editor_decision, exactly as satire.njk does. BE CLEAR ABOUT WHAT THAT
  MEANS NOW: since AUTO_APPROVE (run.py, the editor's standing instruction of 2026-10-08 to
  publish everything) `editor_decision` records "falls under a standing instruction", NOT "a
  person read this one". So a brief reaches this page on the next build without anyone having read
  it, and a `blocked` gate does not hold it back -- it travels with its flags shown instead.

  That is the editor's settled choice for the news products and it is not this file's place to
  override it. It is worth stating here only because THIS desk's risk profile is different from
  the products the instruction was written for: the satire desk mocks politicians, who hold power
  on the public's behalf, while this one reads ALL the news, so its window holds deaths,
  accidents, charges, children and asylum cases. The template's rule -- hit the institution, the
  euphemism or the arrangement, never the person a story happened to -- held in both of the first
  two runs, but it holds because a model followed an instruction.

  If that ever needs to change, the switch is AUTO_APPROVE=0, which restores per-report review for
  every desk; there is no per-product setting today.
#}
{% set drafted = reports | where("product", "vitsedesken") %}
{% set approved = drafted | where("decision", "approved") %}

<p class="sub">{{ site.t.comedyNote[0] }}
<span class="alt">{{ site.t.comedyNote[1] }}</span></p>

{% if not approved | length %}
  <p class="body empty">{{ site.t.noComedy[0] }}<br>{{ site.t.noComedy[1] }}</p>
  {% if drafted | length %}
  <p class="sub">{{ drafted | length }} {{ site.t.comedyWaiting[0] }}
  <span class="alt">{{ drafted | length }} {{ site.t.comedyWaiting[1] }}</span></p>
  {% endif %}
{% else %}
  {# Latest approved in full; the rest as an archive list, so the section keeps working as it
     grows rather than becoming one endless page. Same shape as satire.njk on purpose -- a reader
     moving between the two sections should not have to learn a second layout. #}
  {% from "digest.njk" import digest %}
  {{ digest(approved | first, site, linkBase, site.internal, images) }}

  {% set older = approved | drop(1) %}
  {% if older | length %}
  <h2 class="day">{{ site.t.earlier[0] }} / {{ site.t.earlier[1] }} · {{ older | length }}</h2>
  <ul class="browse briefs">
  {% for r in older %}
    <li><a href="{{ linkBase }}digest/{{ r.slug }}/">
      <span>{{ r.headline_en or r.headline }}</span>
      <span class="n">{{ r.day }}</span></a></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
